# Chrome DevTools MCP - Browser Automation & Debugging

**MCP Server Name**: `chrome-devtools`

## When to Use
- Navigate to ACM/OpenShift console URLs
- Check UI elements, buttons, page behavior
- Investigate RBAC visibility issues
- Debug Fleet Virtualization tree view or VM actions
- Analyze network requests to ACM API
- Check console errors or JavaScript issues
- Find DOM selectors for Cypress test automation

## Available Tools

| Category | Tools |
|----------|-------|
| **Navigation** | `navigate_page`, `new_page`, `close_page`, `list_pages`, `select_page`, `wait_for` |
| **Input** | `click`, `fill`, `hover`, `press_key`, `drag`, `upload_file`, `handle_dialog`, `fill_form` |
| **Debugging** | `take_screenshot`, `take_snapshot`, `evaluate_script`, `list_console_messages`, `get_console_message` |
| **Network** | `list_network_requests`, `get_network_request` |
| **Performance** | `performance_start_trace`, `performance_stop_trace`, `performance_analyze_insight` |
| **Emulation** | `emulate`, `resize_page` |

## Exceptions (Use Dedicated Tools Instead)

- NEVER use Chrome DevTools for GitHub pages -> use `gh` CLI
- NEVER use Chrome DevTools for JIRA pages -> use `jira` MCP server

Browser operations via MCP are read-only and do NOT require permission checkpoint.
